## Iterator data types[#](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#iterator-data-types "Link to this heading")
The iterator layout is an internal detail, and user code only sees an incomplete struct. 

typeNpyIter[#](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter "Link to this definition") 

This is an opaque pointer type for the iterator. Access to its contents can only be done through the iterator API. 

typeNpyIter_Type[#](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter_Type "Link to this definition") 

This is the type which exposes the iterator to Python. Currently, no API is exposed which provides access to the values of a Python-created iterator. If an iterator is created in Python, it must be used in Python and vice versa. Such an API will likely be created in a future version. 

typeNpyIter_IterNextFunc[#](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter_IterNextFunc "Link to this definition") 

This is a function pointer for the iteration loop, returned by [`NpyIter_GetIterNext`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter_GetIterNext "NpyIter_GetIterNext"). 

typeNpyIter_GetMultiIndexFunc[#](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter_GetMultiIndexFunc "Link to this definition") 

This is a function pointer for getting the current iterator multi-index, returned by [`NpyIter_GetGetMultiIndex`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter_GetGetMultiIndex "NpyIter_GetGetMultiIndex").
## Construction and destruction[#](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#construction-and-destruction "Link to this heading") 

[NpyIter](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter "NpyIter")NpyIter_New([PyArrayObject](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/types-and-structures.html#c.PyArrayObject "PyArrayObject")op, [npy_uint32](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/dtype.html#c.npy_uint32 "npy_uint32")flags, [NPY_ORDER](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_ORDER "NPY_ORDER")order, [NPY_CASTING](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_CASTING "NPY_CASTING")casting, [PyArray_Descr](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/types-and-structures.html#c.PyArray_Descr "PyArray_Descr")dtype)[#](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter_New "Link to this definition") 

Creates an iterator for the given numpy array object `op`.
Flags that may be passed in `flags` are any combination of the global and per-operand flags documented in [`NpyIter_MultiNew`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NpyIter_MultiNew "NpyIter_MultiNew"), except for [`NPY_ITER_ALLOCATE`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NPY_ITER_ALLOCATE "NPY_ITER_ALLOCATE").
Any of the [`NPY_ORDER`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_ORDER "NPY_ORDER") enum values may be passed to `order`. For efficient iteration, [`NPY_KEEPORDER`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_ORDER.NPY_KEEPORDER "NPY_KEEPORDER") is the best option, and the other orders enforce the particular iteration pattern.
Any of the [`NPY_CASTING`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_CASTING "NPY_CASTING") enum values may be passed to `casting`. The values include [`NPY_NO_CASTING`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_CASTING.NPY_NO_CASTING "NPY_NO_CASTING"), [`NPY_EQUIV_CASTING`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_CASTING.NPY_EQUIV_CASTING "NPY_EQUIV_CASTING"), [`NPY_SAFE_CASTING`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_CASTING.NPY_SAFE_CASTING "NPY_SAFE_CASTING"), [`NPY_SAME_KIND_CASTING`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_CASTING.NPY_SAME_KIND_CASTING "NPY_SAME_KIND_CASTING"), and [`NPY_UNSAFE_CASTING`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/array.html#c.NPY_CASTING.NPY_UNSAFE_CASTING "NPY_UNSAFE_CASTING"). To allow the casts to occur, copying or buffering must also be enabled.
If `dtype` isn’t `NULL`, then it requires that data type. If copying is allowed, it will make a temporary copy if the data is castable. If [`NPY_ITER_UPDATEIFCOPY`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/c-api/iterator.html#c.NPY_ITER_UPDATEIFCOPY "NPY_ITER_UPDATEIFCOPY") is enabled, it will also copy the data back with another cast upon iterator destruction.
Returns NULL if there is an error, otherwise returns the allocated iterator.
To make an iterator similar to the old iterator, this should work.
```
iter=NpyIter_New(op,NPY_ITER_READWRITE,
NPY_CORDER,NPY_NO_CASTING,NULL);

```
